A||||16||saleenfiero||C6 Prototype with 427 option!!!||||1||
Z||000000||saleenfiero||07-26-2001||01:10 PM||||Anyone who has been following the development of the next gen corvette may have heard the rumor about a very limited edition - GM built lingenfelter 427 corvette to coincide with the release of the C6.  Well, now the rumor has been pretty much confirmed by someone very high up at GM.  Looks like Chevy was very indimidated by the specs on the new viper and decide that the C6 must match the performance of the Gen 3 viper.  this will get interesting.<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||07-26-2001||01:24 PM||||Someone very high up at GM????<P>What I heard from michael black an Engineer on the Corvette team (long time friend of my family's) was that the car's hydroformed frame was designed to accept a 4 cam version of the small block from the start , and that the C6 will eventually use a 4 cam variation of the z06's LS6. The first incarnation of the C6 will use a Ls1-Ls6 variation yet to be named , a better motor won't be seen for 2 years into the production run. (Typical GM)<BR>Micheal also said there still learning the in's and outs of  variable timing from Toyota whom they have several joint ventures on the go with. <P>I have read in some magazines about Lingenfelters own reliability concerns with the cylinder bores of his 427(actually 427.6) LS1. <P>As for keeping up with the Viper , the Zo6 already beats the viper in performance.<P>I have seen a few sketchs and Clay models of the C6 , I like the looks a lot better, does not look like an RX7. I was sad when they rounded everything off , made the car look less "macho" But perhaps I see it that way because of the 18,000 mile 87 Z51 in the garage. Flat grey word challenge (vette) wheels , lowered , borla exhaust and lots of engine mods. Car kinda says Get out of the way ..or I will move you.<P>Gm put a lot of Special cars on permanent hold. Automotive economists see the autoindustry falling flat for the next few years. The 90's were a good time for the auto industry , this has had a profound affect on the sales of this century. People rushed to buy cars in the 90's , consumers don't see the need to buy cars right now. It's predicted that sales will pick up in about 2004. Sales right now are good for the North American market , but they are falling<P>With them fell the idea of the V8 Impala , the Z06 Special edition F body that would close out the F body chapter in history. No plans for a big rear drive Chrysler , PT crusier convert , and beetle convert. All cars that were considered heavily for production. there just isn't a market for it. I think you will see them hold off the C6 for a while too.<P>JM<P>Hope that sets the record straight. I CC'd this to micheal just to make sure I got it right.<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Justin||07-26-2001||01:41 PM||||Z06 beats viper in performance?  Hmmm...Which Viper?  It would only be fair if your going to take the top of the line Z06 Vette to also take the top of the line Viper ACR. <BR>      ........          ......Viper.......    Vette<BR>0-60 mph......         4.1.......      4.3<BR>Top Speed.....        192.......    175 to 180?<BR>Quarter Mile..    12.10.......    12.59<BR>Skid Pad......         .99.......      .98<BR>Slalom .......           75.......      65?<P>As you can see, the Vette isn't far behind, but it's still slower.  As for braking, well, lets wait till the Viper gets ABS in 2002, then we will compare.  But for now, the Vette stops much sooner.  I'm not trying to be a jerk here, but you said the Z06 can beat a Viper, and the Viper is my favorite car, so I have to defend it     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Oh yeah and just so you know, the ACR package only adds 10 hp, changes suspension geometry, and reduces about 100 pounds, so it's not that much of a change from the normal one. The biggest difference is handling.  Nobody but nobody beats a Viper!!!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>If at first you don't succeed, pretend you were never trying in the first place.<P>visit <A HREF="http://www.twinkiesproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.twinkiesproject.com</A>  for information on the chemical properties, reactions, gravitational resonse, and density issues of a Twinkie.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by Justin (edited 07-26-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Justin (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||07-26-2001||02:03 PM||||The top of the line Vette is still a good 30-40 grand less then the Viper RT/10.  I think we comparing the Z06 with the RT/10 viper will suffice.  BTW, how much does that ACR run???||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||07-26-2001||02:08 PM||||yeah dollar for dollar the vette is a faster car. I don't like the looks much of the vette. I have seen off the showroom floor z06's turn 12.4's in the 1/4.. Magazines are a good guideline , but real world is where it's at.<P>Vipers handle like shopping karts. Ask anyone who has autocrossed or raced them. <P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
