Z||000006||saleenfiero||07-26-2001||04:03 PM||||The '02 Z06 can match the vipers acceleration to 60, but the real news is after 60.  The viper still smokes the Z06 all the way to top speed.<BR>Lingnefelter has already addressed the cylinder weakness prob with the 427 engine, by installing something like iron liners or something one the engine to allow it to be bored easily.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||07-26-2001||04:08 PM||||The concern IS with the liners and heat disapation. This news is less than a week old. One of the guys in our club (Runs a 383 supercharged 95 F-body in the one lap of america, he has won it 3 times and run it for 11 years. He is the source of my info , he wanted a N/A 427 LS6 motor , Lingenfelter said to wait (this was 2 weeks or so ago)that he was having issues with the testmule blowing head gaskets , and that they were really at a standstill as to what to do. Besides that My friend who works on the corvette said there are no plans for a 427 Vette built by lingenfelter to be sold as special editions through GM. There is some bad blood between Lingenfelter and GM still over the Hurst joint venture and warranty concerns<P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
